1. What is closure?

=> A function along with its lexical scope bundled together forms a closure.

JavaScript uses lexical scoping, so when a variable is accessed, the engine searches the current lexical environment and then walks outward through 
the scope chain until it finds the variable or reaches the global scope.

And this exact mechanism is the foundation of closures.


